  "task": "transcribe",
  "text": "Being here in Bolonia, it would be logical to finish off these 8 days with a tribute to one of the most extraordinary couples in film music, Hitchcock and Herman. To define a couple such as this one, you must refer to Vitalio Di Cica's answer to when they asked him what one thing does and what the other thing does. To which he would reply, we are like Capuchino. There is milk and there is coffee. We don't know what the milk does and we don't know what the coffee does, but in the end there is Capuchino and that is all that really matters. Herman composed film music for 7 of Hitchcock's most extraordinary films. Their collaboration began in 1955 with the Trouble with Harry and ended in 1964 with Marnie. These are 7 great films and 7 amazing musical compositions. Why did Herman compose these 7 amazing soundtracks? For Hitchcock and why did Hitchcock have such a great relationship with Herman? Tonight we will listen to soundtracks from the man who knew too much, Vertigo, Psycho and North by Northwest. They will be performed by the community orchestra conducted by Timothy Brock. We will see each other at the end and talk some more about the festival and to present",
  "words": null
